    "notes": "ROM-proven HEAD/GET index path: 06EB39; header scan :[MAP at 06EB71 then LF at 06EC64. At 06EBC2 a record starts with m and five skipped characters; 06EBF8 stores a trimmed filename in a 48-byte SRAM slot. The next line scans through = and stores its title in the following slot. 06EC35 treats 1A as EOF. The original display routine 06EC73 uses filename/title pairs and at 06ECE5 fetches up to 0200 bytes of preview data before drawing; it supplies the stored filename verbatim to the bare-GET SDK. Newly authored one-entry M31 PLACEHOLDER index and 512-byte newly drawn M31 DEMO 2bpp preview, not original maps or graphics. Full map selection, game data and original content remain unknown. Parser boundary correction: 06EBC8/06EBCD exits on a non-m record prefix; an extra blank line terminates the list before EOF. Direct EOF in 06EC35 takes 06EC4B RET without restoring its saved DS and DX words and disrupts the native return stack. Blank line is authored syntax, not original recovered index. Preview copy 06EF85/06EF98 transfers 32 2bpp tiles to native graphics RAM; marker glyphs are newly drawn, with no original graphics or playable map supplied."
